# Architecture projects

Projects are data, not HTML. One JSON file per project generates both language versions.

## Files

- Data: `src/_data/projects/[slug].json` (kebab-case slug = file name). URLs: `/projekty/[slug]/` and `/en/projects/[slug]/`.
- Images: `src/images/[slug]/`. Paths in JSON start with `/images/[slug]/`.
- Shape: `{ "pl": {...}, "en": {...} }`, both with `title`, `order`, `category`, `location`, `year`, `summary`, `description` (paragraphs separated by a blank line), `credits`, `images: [{ src, alt }]`. Missing `en` fields fall back to `pl`.

## Rendering

- `src/project.njk` renders project pages; `src/index.njk` renders the homepage slideshow and portfolio cards from `projectList` (sorted by `order`).
- First image = hero and slideshow cover. Remaining images: odd count starts with one full-width image, then pairs; even count is pairs only.
- Images are optimized at build time by `@11ty/eleventy-img`; the lightbox (`src/assets/js/lightbox.js`) uses `currentSrc`.
- Do not hand-write project HTML or edit `sitemap.xml`; both are generated.

## Check

`npm run build && npm test` must pass after any change.
